# Run directories ARE tracked: answers, results, metrics, traces and logs are the
# point of the experiment. Only two things are held back, both from inside the
# per-query isolated Hermes home.

# 1. The isolated home's own files. state.db is a binary SQLite store of exactly
#    the data already tracked as trace/sessions.jsonl, and at ~6 MB per query it
#    would add gigabytes of undiffable blobs. config.yaml is a per-query copy of
#    the user's config (secrets are ${ENV} references, but the redacted
#    config.snapshot.yaml at the run root is the record worth keeping), and .env
#    is a symlink into the live Hermes home.
*/queries/*/hermes_home/*

# 2. ...except the agent's own log files, which are genuine trace material.
!*/queries/*/hermes_home/logs/
